/E (\(EAR\) is calculated by analyzing the distance between specific facial landmarks around the eyes. The vertical distance between the upper and lower eyelid, and the horizontal distance between the left and right corners of the eye, is used to compute this ratio. When the eyes are open, the EAR remains relatively stable, but when the eyes begin to close \(such as during a blink\), the EAR drops significantly. The system monitors these fluctuations to determine whether the eyes are open or closed. By setting a threshold value for EAR, the system can effectively differentiate between normal eye movements and signs of drowsiness, such as when the eyes)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
