/E (In a real-time drowsiness detection system, the webcam serves as the primary input device, capturing live video frames of the driver. The system continuously processes these frames to detect signs of drowsiness or fatigue. To begin, we initialize the webcam by creating a capture object, which connects to the camera and allows the system to access the video feed. The webcam acts as a live input stream, capturing images at a specified frame rate, usually 30 frames per second \(fps\), ensuring that the system can detect changes in real-time. The webcam allows for easy integration into various systems without requiring complex hardware setups, making it ideal for applications like driver monitoring.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [13]
>>
