/E (with approximately 1.25 million deaths annually due to automobile collisions \(WHO, 2015\). In India alone, traffic accidents cause 377 daily fatalities \(equivalent to a jumbo jet crash every day\), of which 40% stem from drowsy driving \(NDTV Research & Central Road Research Institute\). India accounts for 11% of global road deaths despite having just 1% of the world's vehicles - the highest fatality rate worldwide.)
